In a previous discussion, James sought guidance on creating a choropleth map in R Shiny using Leaflet and a shapefile, specifically asking how to color regions based on an attribute. I provided a step-by-step guide, starting with loading necessary libraries (`shiny`, `leaflet`, `sf`, `dplyr`), reading the shapefile with `st_read`, and preparing the data by manipulating the relevant attribute. I suggested structuring a basic Shiny app, outlining the UI and server functions to display the map with colored regions using the `addPolygons` method. Additionally, I noted customization options for color schemes and polygon styling, ensuring James could adapt the example to suit his specific data and visualization needs.
